            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"The believer's assurance and present possession of salvation, as well as the future hope of final deliverance, which protects the mind and spiritual life from doubt and demonic attack.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Ephesians 6:17\",\"1 Thessalonians 5:8\",\"Isaiah 59:17\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Protection of the intellect and thoughts from false doctrine, despair, and deception.\",\"basis\":[\"Ephesians 6:17\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Strictly eschatological hope, focusing on the ultimate, future realization of salvation and deliverance from God's wrath.\",\"basis\":[\"1 Thessalonians 5:8\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The divine warrior's armor, symbolizing God's own victory, vindication, and saving power applied to His people.\",\"basis\":[\"Isaiah 59:17\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"Interpretation is highly stable and stems from Paul's Armor of God metaphor. While academic commentary heavily emphasizes the Old Testament divine warrior roots from Isaiah and the eschatological hope of 1 Thessalonians, pastoral teaching often allegorizes the helmet as psychological or intellectual protection for the believer's mind against spiritual doubt.\"}",
